Alembic migrations for the orchestrator backend.

The database URL comes from the application's Settings (see env.py), never from alembic.ini, so
migrations and the running application cannot disagree about which database they target and no
credential is committed.

  cd backend
  uv run alembic upgrade head          # apply
  uv run alembic downgrade -1          # roll back one
  uv run alembic upgrade head --sql    # review the SQL without connecting
  uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe the change"

tests/test_migrations.py asserts that `upgrade head` produces exactly the schema the models
declare, so a model change without a matching migration fails the suite rather than surfacing as a
runtime error in production.
